  "text": "You guide Mara. Pip waits in Grandma’s garden.\n\nMake someone or something part of an activity.\n\nHarmed or broken so it may not work properly.\n\nWhen something happens, or how long it lasts.\n\nHelp someone find a way or decide what to do.\n\nMaybe; something is possible but not certain.\n\nPip delivered Grandma’s actual story to Mara.\n\nSomething a person adds to a shared activity.\n\nMoving up or down using steps, hands or feet.\n\nSay something to request help or information.\n\nWas suspended, with a part pointing downward.\n\nPip will read Mara’s page while Mara listens.\n\nThe things used to build or repair something.\n\nPut a seed or plant into soil so it can grow.\n\nA choice made after thinking about something.\n\nClick the dock or use the arrow keys to walk.\n\nBelieved something was true without checking.\n\nA small part from which a new plant can grow.\n\nA piece of writing that may still be changed.\n\nThe part of the body with the face and brain.\n\nFit something firmly into its intended place.\n\nM-15-85v-9q-5-10 6-11 8-8 15 0 12-1 10 10v10Z\n\nPreferably; rather hear means prefer to hear.\n\nMade something go to another person or place.\n\nBelonging to the hill, a raised area of land.\n\nThe place where the two bridge sections meet.\n\nAttaching firmly so something stays in place.\n\nMara tells her story to Pip, Sol and Grandma.\n\nValuable or meaningful enough to do or share.\n\nAn enclosed space that heats food for baking.\n\nPlant the seed together before the gathering.\n\nMoving on wheels or by turning over and over.\n\nThe direction from which something is viewed.\n\nRead here, then choose what Pip says or does.\n\nKnows what something means or why it happens.\n\nHave an idea or belief; it may need checking.\n\nLet someone else have, hear or use something.\n\nPip reads Mara’s page. Mara is still at work.",
